To determine how many lassis Caroline can make out of twelve mangoes, we start by finding out how many lassis she can make from one mango. Since she can make eleven lassis from two mangoes, we can calculate the number of lassis per mango as follows:

\[
\text{Lassis per mango} = \frac{11 \text{ lassis}}{2 \text{ mangoes}} = 5.5 \text{ lassis per mango}
\]

Next, we need to find out how many lassis she can make from twelve mangoes. We do this by multiplying the number of lassis per mango by the total number of mangoes:

\[
\text{Lassis from twelve mangoes} = 5.5 \text{ lassis per mango} \times 12 \text{ mangoes} = 66 \text{ lassis}
\]

Therefore, the number of lassis Caroline can make out of twelve mangoes is \boxed{66}

